Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 04:01:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panvk/csf: push constant-offset reads of descriptor-set UBOs
 of fragment shaders to the FAU

rg477m/049 pushes constant-offset reads of dynamic uniform buffers (DXVK's
constant buffers, resource table 0) to the FAU. Native Vulkan and Zink bind
their constants as plain uniform buffers in descriptor sets (tables 1 and
up), whose reads stayed LD_PKA loads through the load/store unit.

The driver now offers the compiler a fragment shader's constant handles of
single, non-update-after-bind UNIFORM_BUFFER bindings (up to 16;
pan_compile_inputs.fau.pushable_set_ubos). bi_opt_push_ubo pushes their
constant-offset reads like table-0 UBOs, naming them UBO
PAN_SET_UBO_ID_BASE + i in the relocations, and now also runs when only
such UBOs are pushable. At each draw the command stream copies the pushed
words from the buffer named by the bound set's host descriptor copy
(a BUFFER descriptor); a set without update-after-bind can't change while a
command buffer uses it, and the copy runs when the draw executes, like the
loads it replaces. Descriptor lowering builds handles from table and index,
so they are constant-folded before the collection.

PANVK_NO_SET_UBO_PUSH=1 keeps those reads as loads.

Purpose: performance: constant-offset reads of plain descriptor-set uniform buffers in fragment shaders (native Vulkan, Zink) become FAU uniform reads instead of LD_PKA loads, as rg477m/049 does for dynamic UBOs; the command stream copies the pushed words from the buffer named by the bound set's descriptor at draw time
Upstream-commit: none
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: applies after rg477m/051 (extends rg477m/049)
Validation test: test build setubo (same code): PanProbe 38/38 x2; Gladius fragment shaders' load/store cycles 120 -> 4 (shaderdb), no shader left at one thread, rendering correct, fps unchanged (on 42.9/44.0/39.9, off 44.0/39.8/43.9); Jupiter Hell (GL via Zink) tutorial on 49.4/50.2 vs off 47.7/48.6 fps (+3.5%); Hades uncapped on 204.9 vs off 206.6 mean of 5 each (noise); vkd3d-proton 2.14.1 suite same as 001-051 except test_sampler_border_color (B27, intermittent: 20 repeats each 7 failures on both 001-051 and this build); gameplay sweep in range: Portal 2 171.4/170.7, Megabonk 69.7, Moonlighter 132.2, ROLLERDROME 91.5, Fallout NV 19.6, Tomb Raider benchmark 74.4, no GPU faults; 16-game boot sweep every game in its known state, no GPU faults; opt-out PANVK_NO_SET_UBO_PUSH=1
Channel: compatibility, unsafe
Generated-by: LLM
